//
// PROBE: `if.in_workbench` and `if.false.in_workbench`, by their own names.
//
// Both take the lambda from the stack. `if.in_workbench` takes its condition
// from the workbench
// (reference/rust_multistackvm/src/stdlib/logic/if_fun.rs:95-97).
// `if.false.in_workbench` passes `StackOps::FromStack`, so despite its name it
// takes the condition from the **stack**
// (reference/rust_multistackvm/src/stdlib/logic/if_fun.rs:103-105). That is
// F2, and Bund2 reproduces it. No golden spells either name.
//
"probe: if.in_workbench runs when the workbench holds true" println
true . { "if.in_workbench ran" println } if.in_workbench
false . { "must not run" println } if.in_workbench
"probe: if.false.in_workbench reads its condition from the stack (F2)" println
false { "if.false.in_workbench ran" println } if.false.in_workbench
debug.display_workbench
